  "id": "xalatath",
  "name": "Xal'atath",
  "role": "Ranged Assassin",
  "overview": "Xal'atath is a Ranged Assassin who can deal burst damage by hitting an enemy Hero with the center of Shadow Mark and detonating Dark Heart Ritual on them. Unlike many mages, she can Basic Attack while moving. Her attacks deal substantial Physical Damage even to frontline Heroes and charge Void Volley, so she can keep dealing damage between Ability casts.\n\nXal'atath is very fragile and has only Void Step to escape. Its long, telegraphed teleport sequence gives enemies time to react, while she must keep using Basic Attacks to charge Void Volley. Although she is difficult to play safely, her mix of good Physical Damage from Basic Attacks and burst damage from Void Volley and her other Abilities is hard for enemies to mitigate, making her rewarding when played well.",
  "strengths": [
    "Great burst damage",
    "Has great area of effect damage",
    "Excellent late game scaling",
    "Can reposition with Void Step",
    "Can stall channeled Objectives with Dark Heart Ritual"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Very fragile",
    "Vulnerable to hard engages",
    "Steep learning curve",
    "Burst depends on landing delayed skillshots",
    "Struggles against highly mobile Heroes"
  ],
