    {
      "name": "Void Volley Build",
      "label": "Situational",
      "description": "The Void Volley Build maximizes Xal'atath's burst damage and adds utility through Dark Heart's Protection's Silence. It works best with allied crowd control, which helps stack Void Adept and Void Volley. Keep Basic Attacking anything in range to charge Void Volley, then use it to hit enemy Heroes whenever possible. Reaching its first 20 Quest stacks is essential for this Build.\n\nIf your Tank has reliable crowd control, spend the early game using only Basic Attacks and Void Volley until they catch an enemy Hero. Then follow up with Shadow Mark and Dark Heart Ritual to detonate the Dark Heart on the Marked target.\n\nWithout reliable allied setup, use Dark Heart Ritual on enemy Heroes or Minion waves, then aim Shadow Mark at Heroes leaving its area. In small skirmishes, try Shadow Mark first. If you miss, wait 2 seconds before placing Dark Heart Ritual on the wave. Shadow Mark will be ready roughly 4 seconds later; hitting a Hero with its center lets the previously placed Dark Heart pursue and detonate on them for a Void Adept stack while you clear the wave.",
